\description{
Computes the reference evapotranspiration series of every station of a
station table (hourly or daily records), and from it the two quantities
that the METRIC chain needs: the instantaneous reference ET at given
overpass times (\code{etr_inst}, mm h-1, for the cold anchor condition) and the
daily reference ET of given dates (\code{etr_24}, mm d-1, for the extrapolation
to 24 hours). It orchestrates the derived variables (\code{\link[=ef_es]{ef_es()}},
\code{\link[=ef_ea_rh]{ef_ea_rh()}}, \code{\link[=ef_wind_2m]{ef_wind_2m()}}, \code{\link[=ef_ra_period]{ef_ra_period()}}, \code{\link[=ef_rso]{ef_rso()}}, ...) and the
reference surface functions (\code{\link[=ef_ref_net_radiation]{ef_ref_net_radiation()}},
\code{\link[=ef_ref_soil_heat_flux]{ef_ref_soil_heat_flux()}}, \code{\link[=ef_ref_et]{ef_ref_et()}}) on the values allowed by the
quality control. The choices that are still open decisions of the
specification (WF-09, WF-11, WF-15, WF-16) are explicit arguments without
defaults.
}
\details{
\strong{Hourly records.} For each record, with \eqn{t} the mid-point of the
period: \eqn{R_a}{Ra} of the period with \code{\link[=ef_ra_period]{ef_ra_period()}} (FAO-56 Eq. 28
or ASCE-EWRI Eq. 48; the treatment of sunrise and sunset follows
\code{standard}; day of year of \eqn{t} in UTC),
\eqn{R_{so}}{Rso} with \code{\link[=ef_rso]{ef_rso()}} (Eq. 37, decision WF-12), the air
pressure from the station elevation (\code{\link[=ef_air_pressure]{ef_air_pressure()}}, Eq. 7, decision
WF-05; a measured \code{air_pressure} is not used), \eqn{\gamma}{gamma},
\eqn{e^\circ(T)}{e0(T)} and \eqn{\Delta}{Delta} at the hourly
temperature, the wind at 2 m from \code{height_wind} (Eq. 47), the solar
radiation converted from W m-2 to MJ m-2 h-1 (x 0.0036, FAO-56 Table 3),
then \code{\link[=ef_ref_net_radiation]{ef_ref_net_radiation()}}, \code{\link[=ef_ref_soil_heat_flux]{ef_ref_soil_heat_flux()}} and
\code{\link[=ef_ref_et]{ef_ref_et()}}. Periods with \eqn{R_{so} > 0}{Rso > 0} (with
\code{"low_sun"}: with a sun angle above 0.3 rad) use their own ratio
\eqn{R_s/R_{so}}{Rs/Rso} (limited to the range of the standard inside
the cloudiness term and flagged \code{EF_WS_RS_RSO_LIMITED}); the others use
\code{night_cloudiness}.

\strong{Daily records.} Tmean = (Tmax + Tmin)/2 (Eq. 9), \eqn{e_s}{es} =
mean of \eqn{e^\circ(T_{max})}{e0(Tmax)} and \eqn{e^\circ(T_{min})}{e0(Tmin)}
(Eq. 12), \eqn{\Delta}{Delta} at Tmean, \eqn{R_a}{Ra} with \code{\link[=ef_ra_daily]{ef_ra_daily()}}
(day of year of the record's day), the solar radiation converted from W
m-2 (24-hour mean) to MJ m-2 d-1 (x 0.0864), \eqn{G = 0}{G = 0} (Eq. 42).
A day with \eqn{R_{so} = 0}{Rso = 0} (polar night) has no defined
cloudiness term and gives \code{NA}.

\strong{Daily sums} (option D1 of the specification for hourly records,
decision WF-16): \code{etr_24} is the sum of the 24 hourly depths of the day
(rate in mm h-1 times 1 h), negative values included; FAO-56 (chapter 4)
states that hourly sums over 24 hours generally match the daily
computation for the grass reference, and ASCE-EWRI (2005, p. 45) sums
hourly ETos or ETrs over the 24-hour period and recommends retaining the
negative values; neither source defines the clock of the day (UTC or
local standard time, WF-11). Its use as the daily reference ET of the
METRIC extrapolation is \verb{VERIFICADA (SEBAL-Idaho 2002)}: Waters et al.
(2002), p. 35, Eq. 44, define ETr_24 as the sum of the hourly alfalfa
reference ET of the day (dev/VERIFICATION.md, row 46); the manual does not
define the clock of the day either. For daily records \code{etr_24} is the
daily value of the record (option D2 with daily data).

\strong{Instantaneous reference ET} (decision WF-09): \code{etr_inst} is a rate in
mm h-1. An overpass time outside the time covered by the records of a
station (option O1: from the start of its first period to the end of its
last period; option O3: from its first to its last mid-point) gives \code{NA}
and the flag \code{EF_WS_OVERPASS_OUTSIDE_RECORDS}; inside that range, a
missing record or a missing reference ET gives \code{NA} and \code{EF_INPUT_NA}.

Values are never filled, truncated or corrected: negative reference ET
is kept (\code{EF_WS_ETR_NEGATIVE}). Under \code{qc_policy = "keep_all"} an
impossible value reaches the numeric functions, which raise
\code{earthflux_domain_error}. Missing or unknown choices raise
\code{earthflux_missing_input} or \code{earthflux_unknown_method}; choices that do
not apply to the time step, a record interval that does not match
\code{timestep}, or a missing column raise \code{earthflux_input_error}
subclasses.
}
\section{Verification status}{

The physics is that of the functions called (FAO-56 grass and ASCE-EWRI
2005 short and tall reference: \code{VERIFICADA}), reproduced through this
function for FAO-56 examples 18 and 19. The orchestration choices are
recorded in the provenance: \code{"before_sunset"} follows FAO-56 (chapter 4)
with the selection of the last qualifying period as an implementation
choice; \code{"low_sun"} (ASCE-EWRI Eq. 46) and \code{"rn_positive"} (ASCE-EWRI
p. 5) are \code{VERIFICADA}; the day definition and the completeness rule are
open decisions (WF-11); the daily sum of the hourly values (D1) is the
ETr_24 of Waters et al. (2002, Eq. 44), \verb{VERIFICADA (SEBAL-Idaho 2002)}
(dev/VERIFICATION.md, row 46). The worked
examples of ASCE-EWRI (2005), Appendix C, are not reproduced: the copy of
the report that was read does not include the appendices.
}

\examples{
# One synthetic station (fictitious values), 48 hourly records in UTC.
times <- as.POSIXct("2024-01-15 01:00", tz = "UTC") + 3600 * (0:47)
mid <- as.numeric(times) / 3600 - 0.5
sun <- pmax(0, cos((mid \%\% 24 - 16.8) * pi / 12))
st <- ef_station_table(
  stations = data.frame(station_id = "ST01", lon = -71.5, lat = -35.4,
                        elevation = 150, height_wind = 2,
                        height_temp_rh = 2),
  observations = data.frame(
    station_id = "ST01", timestamp = times,
    air_temperature = 14 + 12 * sun, relative_humidity = 80 - 45 * sun,
    wind_speed = 1 + 2 * sun, solar_radiation = 850 * sun
  ),
  provenance = list(timestamp_convention = "end", interval = 3600,
                    crs = "EPSG:4326")
)
et <- ef_station_ref_et(
  st, reference = "alfalfa", timestep = "hourly", standard = "asce",
  humidity = "relative_humidity", day_definition = "utc",
  day_completeness = "all_periods", daytime_rule = "rn_positive",
  night_cloudiness = "low_sun",
  overpass = as.POSIXct("2024-01-15 14:48", tz = "UTC"),
  inst_method = "O3"
)
et$etr_inst
et$etr_24
}
